   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "וְאִם אָמַר לָהּ עַל מְנָת שֶׁתֹּאמְרִי. וְתֵימָא? אָמַר רַב יְהוּדָה אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל: דְּבָרִים שֶׁל קָלוֹן.",
   "en": "§ The mishna stated: «And if he said to her:» The vow will be void «on condition that you tell» so-and-so what you told me, or what I told you, he must divorce her and give her the payment of her marriage contract. The Gemara asks: «And let her say it.» Why shouldn’t she simply comply with his wishes? «Rav Yehuda said» that «Shmuel said:» It is referring to «degrading matters,» meaning intimate conversations between husband and wife, which she is ashamed to relate in the presence of others."
  }
